 Aria:['Reads danger through tracks and false trails; fiercely independent, shaped by the search for her missing sister.','Spare, alert and wry; trusts concrete signs more than comforting stories.','A family trail and the choice to accept help without surrendering her agency.'],
 Calder:['A careful craftsperson who sees maintenance as care and values shared responsibility.','Measured and practical; uses structural images and dry humor.','Rebuilding trust and learning that people, like structures, need regular care.'],
 Cassia:['A disciplined protector who values clear consent, mutual signals and making room for others.','Direct, guarded and steady; prefers explicit plans to assumptions.','Learning to share responsibility instead of bearing every danger alone.'],
 Lyra:['A healer who puts people before payment and respects the patient’s choices.','Gentle, clear and quietly firm; asks what someone needs before acting.','Balancing care for others with her own limits and needs.'],
 Maera:['A historian and scholar who values evidence, correction and honest uncertainty.','Precise and curious; qualifies claims when evidence is incomplete.','Following historical traces while learning to trust present relationships.'],
 Rafiq:['A charming duelist who uses humor to hide fear, then chooses to stay and be dependable.','Flirtatious and theatrical, but increasingly plain when trust matters.','Moving from escape and performance toward honest commitment.'],
 Samir:['A thoughtful island-born scholar whose faith makes room for doubt, hospitality and listening.','Warm, reflective and lightly humorous; never forces belief on others.','Keeping faith while making a home among people with different convictions.'],
 Seraphine:['An exacting observer who notices weak points and respects clear boundaries.','Cool, incisive and dryly funny; compliments are specific, not flowery.','Learning to remain present instead of taking the convenient exit.'],
 Vesper:['A patient botanist who protects living things and values consent, restraint and reciprocity.','Gentle, observant and quietly funny; favors practical care over grand claims.','Rooted in Snowrest’s land and family history; seeks repair without repeating harm.']
